{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Of Benjamin he said.</b> Since the blessing of Levi is in the sacrificial service and that of Benjamin in the building of the Temple — in his portion, they are adjacent to each other — and Joseph is placed after him, because the Tabernacle of Shiloh too was built in his portion, as it says ״וַיִּמְאַס בְּאֹהֶל יוֹסֵף״ (Psalms 78) — and because the eternal House is dearer than Shiloh, therefore Benjamin was placed before Joseph." "<b>He shelters him.</b> Covers him and shields him." "<b>All the day.</b> Forever — since Jerusalem was chosen, the Shechinah has not dwelt in any other place." "<b>And between his shoulders he dwells.</b> The Temple was built on the height of his land, except that it was twenty-three cubits lower than Ein Eitam, and there David's intention was to build it, as is found in שְׁחִיטַת קָדָשִׁים (Zevachim 54). They said: a cape was placed on it, because it is written ״וּבֵין כְתֵפָיו שָׁכֵן״ — you have nothing finer on an ox than its shoulders."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:44.047629353Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}